# Keep GitHub's auto-generated "Source code (zip/tar.gz)" archives lean: strip
# developer-process material that end users don't want. `git archive` (which is
# what GitHub uses for tag/release archives) honors export-ignore; the paths stay
# in the repo for anyone who clones. The curated release asset (dist/pxx-<tag>.tar.gz,
# built by tools/release.sh) is separate and already excludes all of this.
#
# NOTE: git archive reads the .gitattributes of the tree being archived, so this
# file must exist in the tagged commit to take effect.

# The BOARD files are fully generated from the ticket files (tools/progress.sh
# board-md) and every lane regenerates them constantly, so a merge/rebase "both
# modified" on one is pure noise. The `ours` merge driver keeps the current side
# instead of conflicting; the content self-heals the next time the board is
# regenerated.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-30, over the previous 12h of origin/master (864 commits):
#   BOARD-brief.md  206 commits   <-- the MOST-touched, and it was NOT covered
#   BOARD.md        198 commits
#   BOARD-done.md   102 commits
# 227 of 864 commits (26%) touch a generated board, which is what makes this the
# conflict majority across eight concurrent lanes rather than an annoyance. The
# glob is deliberate: the original line named BOARD.md when that was the only
# board, and BOARD-brief.md -- added later, and now the busiest of the three --
# inherited none of its protection. Name the class, not the file that existed.
#
# THE DRIVER MUST BE REGISTERED PER CHECKOUT; git config is not committable, and
# an unregistered driver makes this line silently inert (that is how it sat from
# the day it was written until 2026-08-30). tools/sync.sh registers it on every
# run, so a clone that has ever synced is covered. By hand:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
devdocs/progress/BOARD*.md merge=ours

agents/               export-ignore
thesises/             export-ignore
library_candidates/   export-ignore
benchmarks/           export-ignore
# Dev bootstrap binaries (Track B's pinned stable, ~65M) — a release ships
# freshly-built pxx-<arch> instead, so keep this dev-only artifact out.
stable_linux_amd64/   export-ignore
CLAUDE.md             export-ignore
.gitattributes        export-ignore
.github/              export-ignore
